# corpus-home tolerance suite — arming-posture sentinel
#
# This committed marker declares WHICH POSTURE the repository asserts for the
# corpus-home adapter tolerance suite, release/tools/tests/test_corpus_home_tolerance.sh.
# The suite derives the posture it OBSERVES from its own structural arming
# detector and compares the two; its rule R8 fails on any divergence, in either
# direction. Without this file the suite is stateless — "the seam has not landed
# yet" and "the seam landed and conforms" are both green, so a revert between
# them is unobservable and the loss of CH-1/CH-2/CH-4 coverage goes unrecorded.
#
# This is a DIFFERENT AXIS from the .enforce sentinels beside it. Those declare
# whether a red verdict BLOCKS (warn | enforce). This one declares whether the
# graded property is APPLICABLE YET. The two vocabularies are disjoint on
# purpose; do not cross them.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is the posture token:
#   pending   the instance-aware corpus-home seam has NOT landed. The suite is
#             expected to report PENDING-SEAM, and its tolerance rules R3/R4/R7
#             are legitimately dormant.
#   armed     the seam HAS landed. The suite is expected to report
#             PASS-SEAM-LANDED, and those rules are actively grading.
#
# The token is neither optional nor inferred:
#   * a change that LANDS the seam MUST flip this token to `armed` in that same
#     change — the suite fails until it does, which is what makes the reverse
#     failure reachable at all;
#   * a change that REVERTS the seam MUST flip it back to `pending` in that same
#     change — an un-arm is permitted, an UNRECORDED un-arm is not;
#   * an absent, empty, or unrecognised token FAILS CLOSED. Deleting this file
#     does not restore the pre-sentinel behaviour; it reddens the suite.
#
# Retiring the suite's PENDING-SEAM branch (see the "Retirement condition" in
# release/references/standards/corpus-home-adapter-constraints.md section 5)
# removes this file and rule R8 together. Neither outlives the other.
armed
